export const ATKINSON_ATTRIBUTION =
  "The title page names no author, only 'Three Initiates', and the book is usually attributed to William Walker Atkinson (1862–1932), a New Thought writer of Chicago. The evidence is the publisher's: the copyright was registered on June 13, 1908 by 'The Yogi publication society, Chicago' (Catalog of Copyright Entries, 1908, entry 15439), not by a person, and the same register lists books by 'Yogi Ramacharaka' copyrighted by the same society in the same weeks; at a Post Office hearing of 4 April 1919 an inspector reported that the society 'was founded by William Walker Atkinson', that its later owner had bought the business from him, and that its owner's husband said 'Yogi Ramacharaka' was 'no such person'. Neither document names the author of the Kybalion; the attribution rests on that ownership and on the book's matter and style, and is argued most fully by Philip Deslippe (2011).";

